Today I solved leetcode question number 1701: Average Waiting Time.
Description: We are given an array of customers where it contains a pair.
              First number of pair is arrival time of customer and another one is the time it requires our chef to make their order.
              We have a chef who takes one order at a time.
              We want to find average waiting time of each customer.
Solution : First we create 2 variables. One being ans and another being curr time.
            When we start for loop first we take curr time as maximum of either curr or customer arrival time at current index.
            Then we can add order time of that customer to our curr variable.
            Then we can add to ans the total waiting time of current customer by simply subtracting the curr time with arrival time of the customer.
            At the end we can return the ans after dividing it by total customers i.e size of array.
